_:b115 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#nil> .
_:b116 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> "The function I so defined is called an improper integral of the second kind and is denoted by the symbol" .
_:b116 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#nil> .
_:b117 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> "10.23" .
_:b117 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#nil> .
_:b118 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> "f(n) increasing" .
_:b118 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> _:b119 .
_:b119 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> "$f(n)\nearrow$" .
_:b119 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#nil> .
_:b12 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> "A series $\\sum a_{n}$ is called absolutely convergent if $\\sum |a_{n}|$ converges." .
_:b12 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#nil> .
_:b120 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> "We indicate this briefly by writing $f(n)\\nearrow$" .
_:b120 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#nil> .
_:b121 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> "10.3" .
_:b121 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#nil> .
_:b122 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> "improper integral of the first kind" .
_:b122 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#nil> .
_:b123 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> "The function I defined in this way is called an infinite integral, or an improper integral of the first kind" .
_:b123 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> _:b124 .
_:b124 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> "exists and is finite. Otherwise, the integral $\\int_{a}^{\\infty}f(x)dx$ is said to diverge." .
_:b124 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#nil> .
_:b125 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> "10.23" .
_:b125 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#nil> .
_:b126 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> "sequence" .
_:b126 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> _:b127 .
_:b127 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> "nth term of a sequence" .
_:b127 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#nil> .
_:b128 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> "The function value $f(n)$ is called the nth term of the sequence." .
_:b128 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#nil> .
_:b129 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> "10.2" .
_:b129 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#nil> .
_:b13 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> "10.18" .
_:b13 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#nil> .
_:b130 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> "series" .
_:b130 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#nil> .
_:b131 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> "This is an example of what is known as an infinite series" .
_:b131 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#nil> .
_:b132 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> "10.1" .
_:b132 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> _:b133 .
_:b133 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> "10.5" .
_:b133 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#nil> .
_:b134 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> "integral estimate for partial sums" .
_:b134 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#nil> .
_:b135 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> "The area of the shaded region is $\\int_{1}^{n + 1}x^{-1}dx = \\log (n + 1)$" .
_:b135 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#nil> .
_:b136 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> "10.1" .
_:b136 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#nil> .
_:b137 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> "THEOREM 10.11" .
_:b137 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> _:b138 .
_:b138 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> "INTEGRAL TEST" .
_:b138 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#nil> .
_:b139 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> "THEOREM 10.11. INTEGRAL TEST. Let $f$ be a positive decreasing function, defined for all real $x \\geq 1$ ." .
_:b139 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> _:b140 .
_:b14 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> "which tells us that the alternating harmonic series has the sum log 2" .
_:b14 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> _:b15 .
_:b140 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> "Then both sequences $\\{s_n\\}$ and $\\{t_n\\}$ converge or both diverge." .
_:b140 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#nil> .
_:b141 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> "10.13" .
_:b141 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#nil> .
_:b142 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> "THEOREM 10.14" .
_:b142 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> _:b143 .
_:b143 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> "Leibniz's rule for alternating series" .
_:b143 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#nil> .
_:b144 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> "If $\\{a_n\\}$ is a monotonic decreasing sequence with limit 0, then the alternating series $\\sum_{n=1}^{\\infty} (-1)^{n-1} a_n$ converges" .
_:b144 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> _:b145 .
_:b145 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> "Note that Leibniz's rule for alternating series is merely the special case in which $x = -1$" .
_:b145 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#nil> .
_:b146 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> "10.17" .
_:b146 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> _:b147 .
_:b147 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> "10.19" .
_:b147 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#nil> .
_:b148 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> "THEOREM 10.9" .
_:b148 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> _:b149 .
_:b149 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> "LIMIT COMPARISON TEST" .
_:b149 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#nil> .
_:b15 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> "The convergence of this series to the sum log 2 was shown in Section 10.17." .
_:b15 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#nil> .
_:b150 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> "Then $\\sum a_{n}$ converges if and only if $\\sum b_{n}$ converges." .
_:b150 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> _:b151 .
_:b151 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> "However, if $\\lim_{n\\to \\infty}a_n / b_n = 0$ , we conclude only that convergence of $\\sum b_{n}$ implies convergence of $\\sum a_{n}$ ." .
_:b151 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#nil> .
_:b152 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> "10.12" .
_:b152 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#nil> .
_:b153 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> "limit comparison test for improper integrals" .
_:b153 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#nil> .
_:b154 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> "THEOREM 10.25. LIMIT COMPARISON TEST. Assume both proper integrals" .
_:b154 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> _:b155 .
_:b155 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> "then both integrals $\\int_{a}^{\\infty}f(x)dx$ and $\\int_{a}^{\\infty}g(x)dx$ converge or both diverge." .
_:b155 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#nil> .
_:b156 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> "10.23" .
_:b156 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#nil> .
_:b157 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> "limit L of {f(n)}" .
_:b157 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#nil> .
_:b158 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> "we must extend the limit concept to sequences. This is done as follows." .
_:b158 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#nil> .
_:b159 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> "10.2" .
_:b159 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#nil> .
_:b16 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> "10.17" .
_:b16 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> _:b17 .
_:b160 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> "Mercator's series" .
_:b160 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> _:b161 .
_:b161 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> "power series for log(1+x)" .
_:b161 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#nil> .
_:b162 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> "it turns out that the logarithmic series in (10.32) is valid at the endpoint $x = +1$ as well" .
_:b162 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#nil> .
_:b163 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> "10.8" .
_:b163 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#nil> .
_:b164 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> "Monotonic sequences are pleasant to work with because their convergence or divergence is particularly easy to determine." .
_:b164 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#nil> .
_:b165 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> "10.3" .
_:b165 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#nil> .
_:b166 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> "THEOREM 10.6" .
_:b166 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> _:b167 .
_:b167 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> "nth-term test" .
_:b167 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> _:b168 .
_:b168 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> "necessary condition for convergence" .
_:b168 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#nil> .
_:b169 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> "THEOREM 10.6. If the series $\\sum a_{n}$ converges, then its nth term tends to 0; that is," .
_:b169 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> _:b170 .
_:b17 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> "10.21" .
_:b17 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#nil> .
_:b170 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> "That is, if the terms $a_{n}$ of a series $\\sum a_{n}$ do not tend to zero, then the series must diverge." .
_:b170 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#nil> .
_:b171 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> "10.11" .
_:b171 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#nil> .
_:b172 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> "The function values $I(b)$ play the role of the “partial sums” and may be referred to as “partial integrals.”" .
_:b172 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#nil> .
_:b173 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> "10.23" .
_:b173 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#nil> .
_:b174 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> "partial sums s_n" .
_:b174 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#nil> .
_:b175 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> "This is called the nth partial sum of the series." .
_:b175 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#nil> .
_:b176 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> "10.1" .
_:b176 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> _:b177 .
_:b177 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> "10.5" .
_:b177 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#nil> .
_:b178 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> "one-to-one mapping of P onto itself" .
_:b178 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#nil> .
_:b179 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> "Such a function $f$ is called a permutation of $\\mathbf{P}$ , or a one-to-one mapping of $\\mathbf{P}$ onto itself." .
_:b179 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#nil> .
_:b18 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> "These are called alternating series and they have the form" .
_:b18 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#nil> .
_:b180 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> "10.21" .
_:b180 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#nil> .
_:b181 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> "formula (10.59)" .
_:b181 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#nil> .
_:b182 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> "More specifically, define $a_{n}^{+}$ and $a_{n}^{-}$ as follows:" .
_:b182 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#nil> .
_:b183 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> "10.21" .
_:b183 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#nil> .
_:b184 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> "THEOREM 10.21" .
_:b184 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#nil> .
_:b185 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> "THEOREM 10.21. Given a series $\\sum a_{n}$ of real terms, define $a_{n}^{+}$ and $a_{n}^{-}$ by (10.59)." .
_:b185 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#nil> .
_:b186 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> "10.21" .
_:b186 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#nil> .
_:b187 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> "real power series" .
_:b187 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> _:b188 .
_:b188 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> "coefficients of a power series" .
_:b188 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#nil> .
_:b189 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> "If x and all the coefficients are real, the series is called a real power series." .
_:b189 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#nil> .
_:b19 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> "10.17" .
_:b19 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#nil> .
_:b190 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> "10.8" .
_:b190 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#nil> .
_:b191 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> "To distinguish the integrals of Chapter 1 from improper integrals, the former are often called “proper” integrals." .
_:b191 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#nil> .
_:b192 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> "10.23" .
_:b192 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#nil> .
_:b193 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> "Let $\\sum a_{n}$ be a series of positive terms. Prove Raabe's test: If there is an $r > 0$ and an $N \\geq 1$ such that" .
_:b193 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> _:b194 .
_:b194 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> "Two important examples known as Raabe's test and Gauss' test are described in Exercises 16 and 17 of Section 10.16." .
_:b194 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#nil> .
_:b195 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> "10.15" .
_:b195 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> _:b196 .
_:b196 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> "10.16" .
_:b196 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#nil> .
_:b197 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> "Zeno's paradox" .
_:b197 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> _:b198 .
_:b198 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> "the racecourse paradox" .
_:b198 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#nil> .
_:b199 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> "One of these, often called the racecourse paradox, may be described as follows:" .
_:b199 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#nil> .
_:b2 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> "Let $\\{a_n\\}$ and $\\{b_n\\}$ be two sequences of complex numbers, and let" .
_:b2 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> _:b3 .
_:b20 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> "THEOREM 10.10" .
_:b20 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#nil> .
_:b200 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> "10.1" .
_:b200 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#nil> .
_:b201 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> "THEOREM 10.13" .
_:b201 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> _:b202 .
_:b202 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> "RATIO TEST" .
_:b202 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#nil> .
_:b203 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> "THEOREM 10.13. RATIO TEST. Let $\\sum a_{n}$ be a series of positive terms such that" .
_:b203 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> _:b204 .
_:b204 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> "Warning. If the test ratio $a_{n+1}/a_{n}$ is always less than 1, it does not necessarily follow that the limit L will be less than 1." .
_:b204 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#nil> .
_:b205 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> "10.15" .
_:b205 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#nil> .
_:b206 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> "THEOREM 10.20" .
_:b206 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#nil> .
_:b207 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> "Then every rearrangement of $\\sum a_{n}$ also converges absolutely and has sum $S$" .
_:b207 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> _:b208 .
_:b208 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> "The hypothesis of absolute convergence in Theorem 10.20 is essential." .
_:b208 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#nil> .
_:b209 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> "10.21" .
_:b209 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#nil> .
_:b21 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> "THEOREM 10.10. Two series $\\sum a_{n}$ and $\\sum b_{n}$ with terms that are positive and asymptotically equal converge together or they diverge together." .
_:b21 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#nil> .
_:b210 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> "then the series $\\sum b_{n}$ is said to be a rearrangement of $\\sum a_{n}$" .
_:b210 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> _:b211 .
_:b211 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> "The foregoing example shows that rearrangement of the terms of a convergent series may alter its sum." .
_:b211 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#nil> .
_:b212 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> "10.21" .
_:b212 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#nil> .
_:b213 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> "recursive definition of a sequence" .
_:b213 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#nil> .
_:b214 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> "Another common way to define a sequence is by a set of instructions which explains how to carry on after a given start." .
_:b214 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#nil> .
_:b215 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> "10.2" .
_:b215 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#nil> .
_:b216 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> "THEOREM 10.22" .
_:b216 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#nil> .
_:b217 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> "Let $\\sum a_{n}$ be a conditionally convergent series of real terms, and let $S$ be a given real number." .
_:b217 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#nil> .
_:b218 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> "10.21" .
_:b218 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#nil> .
_:b219 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> "THEOREM 10.12" .
_:b219 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> _:b220 .
_:b22 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> "10.12" .
_:b22 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#nil> .
_:b220 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> "ROOT TEST" .
_:b220 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#nil> .
_:b221 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> "THEOREM 10.12. ROOT TEST. Let $\\sum a_{n}$ be a series of nonnegative terms such that" .
_:b221 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> _:b222 .
_:b222 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> "To prove (b), we observe that R > 1 implies $a_{n} > 1$ for infinitely many values of n and hence $a_{n}$ cannot tend to 0." .
_:b222 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#nil> .
_:b223 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> "10.15" .
_:b223 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#nil> .
_:b224 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> "subscript notation a_n" .
_:b224 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#nil> .
_:b225 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> "Very often the dependence on n is denoted by using subscripts" .
_:b225 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#nil> .
_:b226 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> "10.2" .
_:b226 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#nil> .
_:b227 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> "series having nonnegative terms" .
_:b227 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#nil> .
_:b228 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> "series having nonnegative terms, that is, series of the form $\\sum a_{n}$ , where each $a_{n} \\geq 0$" .
_:b228 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#nil> .
_:b229 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> "10.12" .
_:b229 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#nil> .
_:b23 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> "asymptotic equality" .
_:b23 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#nil> .
_:b230 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> "sum symbol for series" .
_:b230 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> _:b231 .
_:b231 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> "dummy index" .
_:b231 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#nil> .
_:b232 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> "is a “dummy index” and may be replaced by any other convenient symbol" .
_:b232 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#nil> .
_:b233 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> "10.5" .
_:b233 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#nil> .
_:b234 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> "tail behavior of series" .
_:b234 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#nil> .
_:b235 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> "It is easy to prove that the two series $\\sum_{k=1}^{\\infty}a_{k}$ and $\\sum_{k=p}^{\\infty}a_{k}$ both converge or both diverge." .
_:b235 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#nil> .
_:b236 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> "10.5" .
_:b236 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#nil> .
_:b237 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> "telescoping property" .
_:b237 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#nil> .
_:b238 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> "Another important property of finite sums is the telescoping property which states that" .
_:b238 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#nil> .
_:b239 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> "10.7" .
_:b239 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#nil> .
_:b24 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> "DEFINITION. Two sequences $\\{a_{n}\\}$ and $\\{b_{n}\\}$ of complex numbers are said to be asymptotically equal if" .
_:b24 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#nil> .
_:b240 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> "those series $\\sum a_{n}$ for which each term $a_{n}$ may be expressed as a difference of the form" .
_:b240 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#nil> .
_:b241 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> "10.7" .
_:b241 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#nil> .
_:b242 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> "THEOREM 10.1" .
_:b242 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#nil> .
_:b243 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> "Assume $f(n) \\nearrow$ and let $L$ denote the least upper bound of the set of function values." .
_:b243 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#nil> .
_:b244 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> "10.3" .
_:b244 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#nil> .
_:b245 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> "THEOREM 10.2" .
_:b245 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> _:b246 .
_:b246 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> "linearity property of convergent series" .
_:b246 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#nil> .
_:b247 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> "Both additivity and homogeneity may be combined into one property called linearity" .
_:b247 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#nil> .
_:b248 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> "10.6" .
_:b248 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#nil> .
_:b249 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> "THEOREM 10.3" .
_:b249 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#nil> .
_:b25 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> "10.12" .
_:b25 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#nil> .
_:b250 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> "Theorem 10.2 has an interesting corollary which is often used to establish the divergence of a series." .
_:b250 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#nil> .
_:b251 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> "10.6" .
_:b251 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#nil> .
_:b252 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> "THEOREM 10.4" .
_:b252 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#nil> .
_:b253 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> "Then the series $\\sum a_{n}$ converges if and only if the sequence $\\{b_n\\}$ converges, in which case we have" .
_:b253 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#nil> .
_:b254 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> "10.7" .
_:b254 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#nil> .
_:b255 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> "THEOREM 10.5" .
_:b255 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#nil> .
_:b256 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> "If $|x| \\geq 1$ , the series diverges." .
_:b256 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#nil> .
_:b257 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> "10.8" .
_:b257 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#nil> .
_:b26 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> "formulas (10.9) through (10.13)" .
_:b26 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#nil> .
_:b27 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> "You may use formulas (10.9) through (10.13) listed at the end of Section 10.2." .
_:b27 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#nil> .
_:b28 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> "10.2" .
_:b28 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#nil> .
_:b29 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> "binomial series (special case)" .
_:b29 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#nil> .
_:b3 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> "Abel's formula is analogous to the formula for integration by parts" .
_:b3 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#nil> .
_:b30 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> "where x is an arbitrary real number, n is a nonnegative integer, and $\\binom{n}{k}$ is the binomial coefficient." .
_:b30 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#nil> .
_:b31 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> "10.1" .
_:b31 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#nil> .
_:b32 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> "THEOREM 10.7" .
_:b32 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#nil> .
_:b33 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> "THEOREM 10.7. Assume that $a_{n} \\geq 0$ for each $n \\geq 1$ ." .
_:b33 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> _:b34 .
_:b34 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> "If the partial sums are bounded above by a number $M$ , say, then the sum of the series cannot exceed $M$ ." .
_:b34 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#nil> .
